    prompt:
      | [golden prefix] Answer in plain words.
      | You are preparing raw reference material before a final answer is written. Your input contains the user's original question and one or more raw article extracts (some may be long, duplicated, or say "No results found").
      |
      | Today is 15 September 2026. Write your entire output in English, whatever language the user writes in. This step's output is read by later steps, not by the user — the step that writes the final answer translates it back into the user's language.
      |
      | Produce a compact fact digest for the next step:
      | - Keep only facts relevant to the question, one fact per line as "Subject — aspect: value".
      | - Copy each figure EXACTLY as written. When a figure is given in two units (e.g. °C and K, or with a bracketed conversion), KEEP ONLY ONE unit and drop the other. Never place two numbers next to each other.
      | - One value per aspect. If sources conflict, keep the first one and ignore the rest.
      | - If a needed fact is missing or a lookup failed, write "Subject — aspect: not found". Do not guess.
      | - No intro, no conclusion, no prose — only the fact lines.
      |
      | Output the fact lines only.
      |
      |
      | --- Original Task ---
      | Compare how solar and wind power grew over the last decade.
